Anyway, I just came down to tell you all
it's time to get dressed for church.

16:33.409 --> 16:34.569
Uh- Uh, gee-

16:34.743 --> 16:38.474
Ah, thanks for the invite,
but, uh, Sunday is kind of our "me" day.

16:38.647 --> 16:40.478
Sunday is not a "me" day.

16:40.649 --> 16:44.483
It's a "he" day, and he will strike down
the blasphemers...

16:44.653 --> 16:48.145
...and the disbelievers
with fury and blood-soaked vengeance.

16:50.592 --> 16:53.789
So chop, chop. Washy, washy.

16:57.299 --> 16:59.563
I've said it before and I'll say it again:

16:59.735 --> 17:01.965
Boy, can I pick them.

17:17.519 --> 17:19.384
- Dad?
- What?

17:19.555 --> 17:22.956
I promise I'll work really hard in school
if you can just get rid of her.

17:23.859 --> 17:26.123
- A little religion isn't gonna kill you.
- Oh, really?

17:26.295 --> 17:29.492
What's your definition
of "blood-soaked vengeance"?

17:40.442 --> 17:41.636
Why are you looking at me?

17:41.810 --> 17:45.109
I just don't wanna miss it
when you burst into flames.

17:49.985 --> 17:52.681
Isn't this a beautiful little church,
Charlie?

17:52.855 --> 17:54.948
Oh, yeah, it's great.

17:55.124 --> 17:57.092
Listen, thought maybe after the service...

17:57.259 --> 18:00.194
...you and I could drive around
and look for a nice apartment for you.

18:00.362 --> 18:03.525
Aw. God doesn't want us
to separate, Charlie.

18:03.699 --> 18:07.226
He brought you back into my life
so that we could be together for all eternity.

18:10.272 --> 18:13.400
Um, are those his words or yours?

18:13.575 --> 18:15.668
He speaks through me.

18:16.478 --> 18:17.604
Okay.

18:17.780 --> 18:19.077
Um...

18:19.248 --> 18:21.739
...to whom am I talking now?

18:24.653 --> 18:28.350
Oh. Oh, it's time for the special blessing.
Come on, everyone, let's go.

18:28.824 --> 18:30.724
Right behind you.

18:31.360 --> 18:34.921
Come on, come on.
Blessing time. Blessing time, come on.

18:36.498 --> 18:38.557
This the kind of church
where they hand out crackers?

18:38.734 --> 18:39.758
- Shh.
- I'm hungry.

18:59.254 --> 19:01.188
Relax. It's just us.

19:02.024 --> 19:03.048
Oh.

19:04.259 --> 19:07.524
- Why is your hair all wet?
- They tried to drown me.

19:07.696 --> 19:09.095
No, they didn't.

19:09.264 --> 19:11.164
He managed to get himself baptized.

19:11.333 --> 19:12.357
How did that happen?

19:12.534 --> 19:15.298
People were lining up.
I thought there was food.

19:15.737 --> 19:18.365
Even after they took your clothes
and gave you a white robe?

19:18.640 --> 19:21.507
I figured maybe we were getting ribs.

19:23.645 --> 19:24.669
So where's Berta?

19:25.047 --> 19:28.483
She took a shine to the organ player
and stayed for the senior potluck brunch.

19:28.951 --> 19:31.010
So there was food.

19:31.753 --> 19:33.653
I knew I wasn't crazy.

19:35.123 --> 19:37.683
Aren't you at all concerned
about what happened to Miss Pasternak?

19:37.860 --> 19:41.626
Of course I'm concerned.
I tried to hide, didn't I?

19:43.365 --> 19:47.699
After she realized that you had dumped her
yet again, she had a bit of a meltdown.

19:48.370 --> 19:49.997
There was more to melt?

19:50.172 --> 19:53.300
She was dripping through the cone
when she left the house.

19:54.376 --> 19:56.537
She grabbed all the bills
out of the collection plate...

19:56.712 --> 19:58.407
...and started grinding on the minister.

19:58.814 --> 20:00.475
Oh, okay. No harm, no foul.

20:01.250 --> 20:02.342
How do you figure?

20:02.718 --> 20:04.515
That's how we found her, right?

20:04.686 --> 20:06.415
Dry-humping for dollars.

20:08.056 --> 20:10.524
What happened to all your guilt
about ruining her life?

20:10.993 --> 20:12.858
Oh, I've still got it.

20:13.028 --> 20:15.019
I'm just learning to live with it.

20:15.931 --> 20:17.057
You're unbelievable.

20:17.499 --> 20:19.967
Oh, come on, I tried to do the right thing.

20:20.135 --> 20:21.432
My intentions were good.

20:22.004 --> 20:23.665
That's the funny thing about you.

20:23.839 --> 20:26.399
It doesn't seem to matter
what your intentions are.

20:26.575 --> 20:31.274
Good, bad or indifferent,
everyone around you ends up suffering.

20:32.381 --> 20:34.645
So it's not my fault, right?

20:36.919 --> 20:38.352
Right.

20:38.687 --> 20:41.178
- Come on, I'll buy you a drink.
- I'm really not in the mood.

20:41.356 --> 20:44.621
Oh, relax, it's all over.

20:44.793 --> 20:47.091
Nothing to worry about.
